  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4a95033faff4a4271a77a8f3b84af233, type: 3}
  m_Name: Level 1 Questions
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::HokkienQuizQuestionBank
  questions:
  - question: 'Which of the following means "How do you sell this?"

'
    choices:
    - "\u8001\u677F\u597D"
    - "\u600E\u4E48\u5356\uFF1F"
    - "\u4F60\u8981\u591A\u5C11"
    - "\u8BF7\u95EE\u8FD9\u662F\u4EC0\u4E48\uFF1F"
    choiceExplanations:
    - "This means \u201CHello Boss\u201D, which is a greeting to the stall owner."
    - "This means \u201Chow do you sell this\u201D, used to ask about the price of
      the dish"
    - "This means \u201Chow much do you want?\u201D, used by the vendor to ask how
      much of something the buyer wants."
    - "This means \u201CWhat is this?\u201D, you can use this to ask what others
      are eating or selling."
    correctAnswerIndex: 1
  - question: If you want to ask about what a food is, what do you say?
    choices:
    - "\u8001\u677F\u597D"
    - "\u600E\u4E48\u5356\uFF1F"
    - "\u4F60\u8981\u591A\u5C11"
    - "\u8BF7\u95EE\u8FD9\u662F\u4EC0\u4E48\uFF1F"
    choiceExplanations:
    - "This means \u201CHello Boss\u201D, which is a greeting to the stall owner."
    - "This means \u201Chow do you sell this\u201D, used to ask about the price of
      the dish"
    - "This means \u201Chow much do you want?\u201D, used by the vendor to ask how
      much of something the buyer wants."
    - "This means \u201CWhat is this?\u201D, you can use this to ask what others
      are eating or selling."
    correctAnswerIndex: 3
  - question: "Which of the following is a worship food for \u4E03\u5A18\u5988\uFF1F\n"
    choices:
    - "\u51E4\u68A8\u9165 - pineapple cake"
    - "\u7B52\u4ED4\u7C73\u7CD5 - tube rice pudding"
    - "\u828B\u7CBF\u5DE7 - teamed Taro Cake"
    - "\u767D\u7CD6\u7CBF - fried Sweet Rice Cake"
    choiceExplanations:
    - "Pineapple cake (\u51E4\u68A8\u9165) is one of the most popular Taiwanese snacks.
      It has pineapple and wintermelon filling, with a pastry shell, but it is not
      a worship food for \u4E03\u5A18\u5988."
    - "Tube rice pudding (\u7B52\u4ED4\u7C73\u7CD5) is a Taiwanese dish made with
      glutinous rice. It is steamed with a tube. It is not a worship food for \u4E03\u5A18\u5988."
    - "Steamed Taro Cake (\u828B\u7CBF\u5DE7) is a Taiwanese dish made with taro
      and glutinous rice. It is often shaped like a moon or Moon blocks (wooden or
      bamboo divination blocks). It is a worship food for the Ghost Festival (\u4E2D\u5143\u8282),
      but not specifically a worship food for \u4E03\u5A18\u5988."
    - "Fried Sweet Rice Cake(\u767D\u7CD6\u7CBF) is a fried sticky rice dough served
      with grinded peanuts or sesame. It is a worship food for \u4E03\u5A18\u5988
      (Seven Star), the goddess who protects children that are under the age of sixteen
      and couples. She is also known as \u7EC7\u5973, the weavergirl from Chinese
      mythology, who has fallen in love with the cowherd \u725B\u90CE. They are separated
      by the milky way because they have violated the laws of heaven, and are only
      allowed to meet each other on the seventh day of the seventh month on the lunar
      calendar. This day is celebrated as \u4E03\u5915\u8282 (QiXi Festival), which
      is still celebrated as Valentines."
    correctAnswerIndex: 3
